  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) and the Shiromani Akali Dal (SAD) have reunited to contest the 2027 Punjab Assembly elections, ending a six-year separation. The alliance was formed under the leadership of Sukhbir Badal, who brought the SAD back into the National Democratic Alliance (NDA). Following the announcement, the partnership faced immediate scrutiny from political opponents, including the Aam Aadmi Party (AAP) and the Congress party. Critics have cited past tensions related to historical farm law disputes and questioned the motivations behind the reconciliation. Conversely, representatives from the Punjab BJP have defended the decision, framing the collaboration as a strategic necessity to manage state administration and address ongoing security and legislative concerns. The alliance seeks to present a joint strategy as both parties prepare for the upcoming electoral cycle, though the decision remains a subject of intense public and political debate.",
